      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Saṁyutta Nikāya 22.51 ",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 22.51 "
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "5. Attadīpavagga ",
      "english": "5. Be Your Own Island "
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "Nandikkhayasutta ",
      "english": "The End of Relishing "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "Sāvatthinidānaṁ. ",
      "english": "At Sāvatthī. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "“Aniccaññeva, bhikkhave, bhikkhu rūpaṁ aniccanti passati. Sāssa hoti sammādiṭṭhi. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, form really is impermanent. A mendicant sees that it is impermanent: that’s their right view. "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "Sammā passaṁ nibbindati. ",
      "english": "Seeing rightly, they grow disillusioned. "
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "Nandikkhayā rāgakkhayo, rāgakkhayā nandikkhayo. ",
      "english": "When relishing ends, greed ends. When greed ends, relishing ends. "
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "Nandirāgakkhayā cittaṁ vimuttaṁ suvimuttanti vuccati. ",
      "english": "When relishing and greed end, the mind is freed, and is said to be well freed. "
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "Aniccaññeva, bhikkhave, bhikkhu vedanaṁ aniccanti passati. Sāssa hoti sammādiṭṭhi. ",
